From be2af816dfb9e5498f1ad7fe58d1b0960dcd3e14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: autoresearch <agent@localhost>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:35:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] diar: run_encoder_isolated - sound oracle for the WHOLE
 encoder stack, not just one layer

Extends the run_layer0_isolated idea (previous commits) to all `weights.layers.size()` layers chained in one
isolated graph, as the acceptance test for porting the entire encoder rather than one layer at a time.
encoder_out (EncoderGraph) captures the real production stack's own final output (after all layers, before
final_norm/head) the same way layer0_in/layer0_out already did for one layer, gated the same way
(AUDIOCPP_DUMP_LAYER0, always dumped alongside the per-layer files - no new env var needed for the ground
truth side). AUDIOCPP_ENCODER_ISOLATED triggers the isolated rebuild, writing iso_encoder_out.f32.

Verified on device: byte-identical to production's real 31-layer output on two different clips
(bilingual_multispk_57s.wav at 339 frames, gate_ms_v2.wav at 527 frames). Production path unaffected when the
new env var is unset (confirmed via the existing turns.json byte-identity check).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
